  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member updating from the current app, I want the uploads listed by the old Objective-C rehost screen (`Documents/rehostImages.plist`) imported too, so that no upload history is lost at the update.\n\n### Facts\n\n- The current app @ 87fe0d1c writes `Documents/rehostImages.plist`, an `NSKeyedArchiver` archive of `RehostImage` objects (`Classes/RehostImageViewController.m:43-48, 160-166`; `Classes/Constants.h:88`; class `Classes/RehostImage.m`).\n- LOT-067 imports only `rehostImagesSwiftUI.json` (`LegacyImporter+Steps.swift:208-225`).\n- The archive's keys cannot be guessed (AGENTS §3): `RehostImage`'s `encodeWithCoder:` in the legacy code, plus a real file, give them.\n\n### Steps\n\n1. **Capture (Mac):** from a device or simulator that used the old rehost screen, copy `Documents/rehostImages.plist`. Anonymize it per docs/FIXTURES.md: the hashes in the img3 URLs are personal; keep the structure. Commit it as a fixture, with the field list read from `RehostImage.m`.\n2. **Import step (cloud):** decode the archive in HFRStorage without UIKit (`NSKeyedUnarchiver` with the legacy class name mapped, or a plist walk on Linux). Merge into the upload history (dedupe by full URL, keep the order), as a new LegacyImporter step that runs once. Tests on the fixture.\n\nOperator decision 2026-11-16: yes.\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnothing: the capture of step 1 is merged (#1043)\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
