   "updated_at": "2026-11-17T08:30:18Z",
   "body": "**mac/M1: the capture of step 1 cannot start without you**\n\n- No simulator on the Mac holds a `Documents/rehostImages.plist` (all CoreSimulator containers searched).\n- The iPhone (15 Pro Max) is not connected. Even when it is, `devicectl` reads only the container of an app installed from Xcode, not of the App Store or TestFlight build.\n\nOptions:\n1. 🟢 **Recommended:** make the archive with legacy's own code, with no network. A test host links `Classes/RehostImage.m` @ 87fe0d1c (as the legacy oracle does), archives 3 `RehostImage` objects with fake img3 URLs through the same `NSKeyedArchiver` call as `RehostImageViewController.m:160-166`, and the fixture is that file. The keys and the class name are legacy's own, there are no personal hashes, and nothing is sent anywhere.\n2. A real file from your iPhone: an unencrypted Finder backup, from which I extract only that file and anonymize the img3 hashes (FIXTURES.md, independent check before the push).\n3. The legacy app on a simulator, one upload through the old rehost screen: that is a public write to the image host, so it needs your go and the image to use.\n\nDecision needed (operator)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
